From 39d05f3d2fd8951e4ac792b1098d7b639aebb858 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: GGEZUS <coelho.b.ricardo@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 8 Sep 2026 05:51:07 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 17/18] feat(input): horizontal swipe column-resize mode

New touchscreen-swipe option: horizontal-swipe "move-view" (default,
the animated view scroll) or "resize-column". In resize mode a quick
horizontal swipe drives the existing interactive-resize machinery on
the focused window (the same one Mod+right-click uses): the width
tracks the fingers 1:1 while swiping, stops when they stop, and stays
where they were lifted. Tiled: the focused column; floating: the
focused window. If there is nothing to resize, the swipe falls back
to the animated view scroll.

The swipe grab gains a ColumnResize state that accumulates the
incremental centroid deltas into the cumulative delta the
interactive-resize API expects, and ends the resize on gesture
end/cancel/ungrab. Vertical swipes, taps, flicks and hold-swipes are
untouched.
